# UTC. commerce times from contracts/entrypoints.md §Schedule, which now names all six -- every
# commerce Dataset member gets a line, per S05 (playbook 02-test-discipline.md T10 records a real
# outage from a dataset with a collector and no cron line). Spacing here is a gap rule, not a minute
# rule: each line's gap to the next has to cover how long it runs, which is its sources' min_interval_s
# times how many requests they make. No runtime is written down here -- the test computes it from those
# policy constants so it follows them (contracts/entrypoints.md §Schedule).
0 * * * *   cosmai collect commerce --dataset ranking
# 2026-08-24: was `5 2`. The new engine walks a dataset's sources one after another
# (engine.collect's `for source in sources`) where the archived collector overlapped them, so the
# hourly ranking walk measured 202s against the old 90s -- and one 403/429 widens daisomall's
# interval 30s->60s (Gate._back_off), which makes it 292s. 02:05 left 98s of clearance, then 8s.
# 02:10 leaves 398s. Each product pass covers at most two boards: at most 2 ranking
# requests plus 34 detail requests with one retry each (70, below the 100-request cap).
10 2 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset product --board skincare,makeup
35 2 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset product --board hair,masks
10 3 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset product --board dermo
# The review_low suncare targets need detail-page ingredients. Their 11 requests would take the
# product collection above 100, so keep them in a separate run after review_low.
30 3 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset review_low --board suncare
45 3 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset ingredients
15 4 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset review
45 4 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset review_stats
30 5 * * *  cosmai collect commerce --dataset new_product
